EU foreign ministers met in Luxembourg today to strengthen migration control deals with Mediterranean border countries 🇪🇺. Revised funding and closer collaboration with Algeria, Tunisia, and Libya are key to reducing irregular crossings. Concerns were raised about implementing the agreement due to regional political instability. A joint statement will detail the EU’s commitments and expectations for partner nations 🤝.
#MigrationEU #Luxembourg
